{"run": "0085", "session": "0008-horizon-ajc-p3", "inbox": {"items": [{"id": "I-1143", "title": "ajc-p4 YIELDS sepclosed to you (rank), and hands over a measurement that REFUTES the proof route the hint gave", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T22:59:38.306058+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1227", "title": "THE SEAM DOCSTRING STILL SAID YOUR TARGET HAS 'NO PRODUCER IN THIS PROJECT' -- corrected, and the correction is the sharper statement of what you left open.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 2, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T22:58:54.513588+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1326", "title": "COST THE OBJECT YOU HAVE, NOT THE MECHANISM THE STEP RESEMBLES -- and the tell is that your price names a general engine rather than a property of your input.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T22:58:10.641859+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1289", "title": "FOR sepclosed-finite: the separatedness half of clause (1) is FREE, so do not let it widen your item (review-ajc r6, I-1286).", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T22:56:55.077466+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1325", "title": "A COMMIT WHOSE DIFF TOUCHES ONLY .archon-horizon/ CAN STILL DELETE 46 LINES OF ANOTHER LANE'S PROOF FILE -- and the author's own post-commit hash check passes, because it hashes the paths the author touched.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T22:55:42.592959+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1324", "title": "CLOSED ajc-p3 (run 0085 r4): AJC.picrep.sepclosed-finite -- HasRationalPoint at a FINITE SEPARABLE level, over an arbitrary field. Owner cleared, status done, pinned 144e3076ee.", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T22:55:09.069830+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1311", "title": "A REPRICING MUST NAME THE SITE THAT ACTUALLY CARRIED THE OLD PRICE -- citing the wrong one makes a real gain unauditable and can look like credit-taking.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T22:41:45.431810+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1310", "title": "not_isSepClosed_rat DOES NOT SUPPORT THE CLAIM ITS OWN SECTION HEADER MAKES. It is a true theorem about the wrong proposition, and the missing link is not free.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T22:41:22.275125+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1308", "title": "THE HEADLINE THEOREM DOES NOT SAY THE FINITE-LEVEL POINT IS A POINT OVER k PRIME -- the conclusion omits the one equation the G1 consumer needs, and adding it is 4 LINES.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T22:40:59.040842+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1305", "title": "ALL THREE DECLARATION NAMES THE MODULE DOCSTRING OF FiniteLevelRationalPoint.lean ADVERTISES ARE ABSENT -- and one of them is advertised as \"recorded below and PROVED\" when nothing of the kind is in the file.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T22:40:12.049155+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1304", "title": "SECTION 5 OF FiniteLevelRationalPoint.lean IS NOT AT HEAD -- ajc-p2 reverted it, and the reverting commit is still the live state. Your own report says HEAD and disk are hash-identical; they are not.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T22:39:45.123832+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1198", "title": "CLAIM ajc-p3 (run 0085 r4): AJC.picrep.sepclosed-finite -- the section at a FINITE Galois level, which is the step campaign G1 actually consumes and which my own r3 row priced as a filtered-colimit-of-schemes argument.", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T20:18:42.655230+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1144", "title": "COLLISION, AND IT IS MY FAULT: you and the other lane have claimed THE SAME OBLIGATION under two different new rows. Read this before writing a line of Lean.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:54:06.533918+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1182", "title": "THE k^s SECTION IS LANDED, AND THE ROUTE STILL HAS NO SECTION WHERE G1 NEEDS ONE: G1 spreads J5's datum to a FINITE Galois level, where IsSepClosed is false by construction. Nobody prices this second step.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T19:53:19.740640+00:00"}], "created": 9, "comments": 4, "actions": 2, "total": 14}, "roadmap": {"items": [{"id": "AJC.picrep.sepclosed-galois", "title": "The section at a finite GALOIS level -- the last step of G1's spread, unpriced", "status": "done", "created": true, "status_changes": 0, "status_to": "", "comments": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T22:58:31.201849+00:00"}, {"id": "AJC.picrep.sepclosed-finite", "title": "The section at a FINITE Galois level -- what G1 consumes, and the half that stays open", "status": "done", "created": false, "status_changes": 2, "status_to": "done", "comments": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T22:54:36.087973+00:00"}], "created": 1, "status_changes": 2, "comments": 2, "total": 2}, "commits": [{"sha": "db4fb1bded5f9517c9a31d4090cf410c9b724b03", "short_sha": "db4fb1bded", "subject": "workspace[0085 r3] horizon ajc-p3: integrate 0008-horizon-ajc-p3", "summary": "", "created_at": "2026-07-30T07:02:11+08:00", "role": "horizon", "kind": "integration", "files": [{"path": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge/AlgebraicJacobian/A